olang <version> — :help for help · quit or ^D to exit


olang help

  :help <name>     a function's documentation      :help map, :help collections.heap.push
  :help <module>   a module's functions            :help str, :help collections
  :help <your fn>  your own code's docs            /// comments above a declaration appear here
  :help list       every function, grouped
  :help syntax     language syntax reference
  :help examples   worked examples                 :help tutorials for guided ones
  :help search <q> find functions by keyword

Modules (:help <module> to open one)
  core       str col math json toml re dates time random crypto base64 bytes bigint value
  system     fs os proc http db chan task cell cancel shared weak caps meta testing
  data       ods stats plot csv collections
  via use    cli term ui viz dash colx mathx

REPL
  :env variables    :type <expr> a value's type    :time <expr> wall-clock an expression
  :history this session    :clear screen or environment    :cd :pwd :ls filesystem
  :sh <cmd> or !<cmd> shell    TAB completes    it holds the last printed result

Anything without a leading colon is olang: use collections { heap }, let x = 1, 1 + 1.


═══ Function: len ═══

Description: Returns the length of a list, string, or tuple
Category:    Collection
Syntax:      len(collection)
Returns:     Int

Parameters:
  • collection: List[T] | String | Tuple - The collection to measure

Examples:
  >> len([1, 2, 3, 4])  // 4
  >> len("hello")  // 5

See Also: head, tail


