=== Search Results (20 found) ===

1. FUZZY map_clear (Maps)
   An empty value of the same kind (a map, an object, a parsed JSON object) — for a map, equivalent to #{}.
   Syntax: map_clear(map)

2. FUZZY map_merge (Maps)
   A new value of a's kind (a map, an object, a parsed JSON object) holding both's entries; where keys collide, b wins.
   Syntax: map_merge(a, b)

3. FUZZY map_remove (Maps)
   A new map without key; removing an absent key returns an equal map.
   Syntax: map_remove(map, key)

4. FUZZY map_set (Maps)
   A new map with key bound to value; the original is unchanged, like every                  olang value.
   Syntax: map_set(map, key, value)

5. FUZZY map_set_in (Maps)
   A copy with the value at the end of the key path set: each level a new value of its own kind, a missing level a new map. A level nothing else holds is written in place, as map_set's sole-owner write.
   Syntax: map_set_in(value, keys, v)

6. FUZZY map_update (Maps)
   A copy with key set to f(the old value) — f is given Unit for an absent key. The old value is moved into f when nothing else holds the map.
   Syntax: map_update(value, key, f)

7. FUZZY map_get (Maps)
   The value under key, or Unit () when the key is absent — a missing key is                  not an error. Reads maps, structs, objects, and parsed JSON uniformly.
   Syntax: map_get(map, key)

8. FUZZY map_get_in (Maps)
   The value at the end of a key path, or Unit at the first missing hop — map_set_in's reading half.
   Syntax: map_get_in(value, keys)

9. FUZZY map_get_or (Maps)
   The value under key, or the default when the key is absent — the one-call form of the missing-key-with-default idiom (map_get returns Unit for absence, which unwrap_or cannot take).
   Syntax: map_get_or(map, key, default)

10. FUZZY map_keys (Maps)
   Every key, in the map's order (each where it was first set) — the order entries uses.
   Syntax: map_keys(map)

11. FUZZY map_values (Maps)
   Every value, in the order map_keys reports.
   Syntax: map_values(map)

12. FUZZY par_map (List)
   map fanned out across OS threads: same results in the same order, one worker interpreter per thread (no GIL). The function runs against worker snapshots like spawn, so mutations to enclosing state are not visible to the caller
   Syntax: par_map(list, function)

13. FUZZY col.flat_map (Collections)
   Map then flatten one level.
   Syntax: col.flat_map(list, fn)

14. FUZZY colx.flat_map (colx)
   map f over xs and concatenate the resulting lists
   Syntax: colx.flat_map(xs, f)

15. FUZZY map_filtered (Higher-Order)
   Filter then map in one pass: function applied to each element the                  predicate accepts.
   Syntax: map_filtered(list, predicate, function)

16. FUZZY plot.heatmap (plot)
   a heatmap of the row-major value grid, as an SVG string
   Syntax: plot.heatmap(x_labels, y_labels, rows, title:, x_label:, y_label:, width:, height:, theme:, paper:, ink:, responsive:, interactive:, colors:, vary:, scale:, font_size:, font:)

17. FUZZY map_has_key (Maps)
   Whether key is present — the way to tell an absent key from one stored                  with a Unit value.
   Syntax: map_has_key(map, key)

18. FUZZY map_len (Maps)
   The number of entries (an object's or a parsed JSON object's fields).
   Syntax: map_len(map)

19. EXACT map (List)
   Applies a function to each element in a list, returning a new list
   Syntax: map(list, function)

20. FUZZY result_map (Result)
   Transform the Ok value of a Result using a function, leaving Err values unchanged
   Syntax: result_map(result, function)

